<task id="138" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Make the Access Permission levels real — Standard / Limited / Restricted enforced at read AND write time on every plane; Limited implemented; communications inherit the parent's permission</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27 — owner decisions round 2, grant-model group)</phase>
    <gate>after-135 (CIAM plane routed through the shared veto pipeline)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-path change in the unified evaluator (pre-max suppression), new write-time refusals on the grant endpoints, an ADR-003 contract amendment, a shared UI component, a PCF, and a Dataverse column retirement. Tags bff-api/auth/pcf.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security semantics across three planes plus an ADR amendment (path B). A wrong predicate here either over-grants on Limited records or silently removes direct grants the owner wants kept.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies AccessibleRecordSetService.cs (after task 135 changes it; 136, 137, 141, 142, 143 and 036 also edit it), GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs (task 139 changes it next; 137 and 142 also edit it), ExternalParticipationService.cs (131, 132, 137), and AccessGrantModal.tsx + the TrackingFieldTrio PCF (tasks 139 and 140 also bump them; 066/067 edit the modal). Merge serially and run /conflict-check first.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>135 (and, through 135, 131)</deps>
