  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner round 2 item 3">Scope: every plane (workforce contact, the systemuser plane's contact-grants term, CIAM).
- Effective contact-access mode per root: RESTRICTED if sprk_accesspermission = 100000002. Otherwise DIRECT-ONLY if sprk_accesspermission = 100000001 OR sprk_issecure = true. Otherwise STANDARD.
- An unreadable or unreturned row is RESTRICTED + DIRECT-ONLY (the existing RootRecordFlags.Unreadable direction, NFR-01).
- A null sprk_accesspermission is Standard. That is today's behaviour and is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 A1 / FR-22">Scope: AccessibleRecordSetService.
- Limited MUST reuse the existing pre-max structural suppression: the same predicate that feeds GrantedRightsFor, the standing term and the org-expansion term.
- Do NOT add a post-max subtraction, and do NOT add a second suppression code path.
- The systemuser membership term (ADR-034) is NOT suppressed by Limited, exactly as it is not suppressed by Secure. Internal access is unaffected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner binding: failed-operation messages">Scope: /grant, /invite-and-grant, /invite. Every policy refusal returns ProblemDetails with a stable reasonCode, a human-readable detail and the traceId.
- Policy refusals are HTTP 422 with these BINDING reason codes (tasks 139, 140 and 142 and the modal depend on them): `sdap.access.grant.record_restricted` (a contact or organization grantee, or /invite, on a Restricted record) and `sdap.access.grant.org_grant_direct_only_record` (an organization-wide grant on a Secure or Limited record).
- A flag-read fault is HTTP 503 `sdap.access.grant.policy_unreadable` with a message ("the record's access settings could not be read; nothing was granted"). It is never an unhandled 500, and never reported as record_restricted.
- ⚠️ Today a fault is indistinguishable from a real Secure+Restricted record: GetRootRecordFlagsAsync folds it into the VALUE RootRecordFlags.Unreadable = (true, true) (ExternalParticipationService.cs:591, :608, :619). The write-time check must know which happened. Carry an explicit unreadable marker on RootRecordFlags (the read path keeps treating it as the most restrictive combination), so the refusal message is true.
- A refusal writes no row, creates no contact, provisions no CIAM account and sends no email.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / DelegationRuleFilter">Scope: ordering. The policy check runs INSIDE the handler, after DelegationRuleFilter has established Write. A caller without Write still gets the filter's 403, so the record's access policy is never disclosed to a non-Write caller. The Write rule itself is not changed (task 139 owns the grant model).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11 / WP-1">Scope: the write-time check.
- There is exactly ONE policy decision function, shared by /grant, /invite-and-grant and /invite.
- CreateGrantAsync (the shared grant core) MUST NOT write a row for a root whose policy refuses the grantee kind. Future writers therefore cannot bypass it: task 140's contact-side route, and the "Assigned To" auto-grant function from owner Q5, which is owned by another task.
- The flags come from the existing ExternalParticipationService.GetRootRecordFlagsAsync (batched, fail-closed). Do not add a second flag reader.
- ⚠️ ABSENT KEY = UNREADABLE at write time. GetRootRecordFlagsAsync returns an EMPTY map for any entity type that is not a key of RootFlagSources (`ExternalParticipationService.cs:549-553`, keyed by LOGICAL name: sprk_project / sprk_matter / sprk_workassignment). The evaluator reads flags as `flags.TryGetValue(id, out var f) &amp;&amp; f.IsSecure`, so a missing key means "no veto". If the write-time check passes the wrong name (for example "project", or an entity-set name), or copies that TryGetValue shape, the policy silently allows everything. The check MUST treat a root id missing from the returned map as unreadable (503 policy_unreadable). A test MUST pin that each ExternalGrantRootType maps (via ExternalGrantRoot.LogicalNameFor) to a flag-bearing entity type.
- The refusal is a TYPED result of the core (for example a refusal member on GrantUpsertOutcome, `GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:394`), never an exception. /grant wraps CreateGrantAsync in a catch-all that answers a bare 500 "Failed to create external access record" (`:114-128`), and /invite-and-grant answers 500 after onboarding (`:144-160`). A thrown refusal would become exactly the bare 500 the owner forbade, and on /invite-and-grant it would follow an onboarding the pre-check should have prevented.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-1 / ADR-002 / WP-5">Scope: direct Dataverse writes. Rows created directly in Dataverse (MDA grid, import) bypass the BFF write-time check. The read-time evaluator is the backstop and MUST stay authoritative. Do not weaken or skip any read-time veto or suppression because a write-time check now exists.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012 / FR-14">Scope: the shared modal stays entity-agnostic. Only pcf/TrackingFieldTrio/index.ts knows the raw option integers and the sprk_issecure column. The modal receives the semantic AccessPermissionState only.
- The sprk_issecure read used for GATING fails CLOSED (unreadable → 'limited').
- The existing fetchSecureOwnerInfo DISPLAY read (:945-963) stays fail-soft.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2 item 3 / misalignment 3">Scope: AccessGrantModal.
- Restricted: hide "+ Contact", "+ Organization" and the role-based candidate (contact) rows. "+ User", user rows, their level dropdowns and Add stay ENABLED. Revoke of existing grants stays available (unchanged, :1084-1089). The delegation/auth deny state still blocks everything (unchanged).
- Limited or Secure: hide "+ Organization". "+ Contact", candidates and "+ User" stay enabled.
- There is no standing-grant control in the modal to hide (see background). Correct the module doc comment (:53-64) to describe the actual per-state behaviour, and remove the dead `onSetStandingGrant` wiring (types.ts prop + PCF handler at index.ts:978/:1200) or document why it stays. Leave standing-ROW rendering to task 066.
- Standard: unchanged.
- Each non-standard state shows one MessageBar that explains the rule, following the existing Restricted banner pattern (:1145-1153).
- When the server refuses anyway, the dialog shows the server's detail text, not a generic error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner Q6">Scope: sprk_communication.
- Remove every code reader and writer of sprk_communication.sprk_accesspermission.
- A communication's effective permission is its parent's (via the sprk_regarding{core} ancestor that CoreAncestorResolver stamps, CoreAncestorResolver.cs:77, :96-99). No client or server code may substitute the communication's own value.
- The column is retired by an operator-run script: dry-run by default, idempotent. It removes form, view and PCF-binding references first, then deletes the column.
- The TrackingFieldTrio manifest declares `accessPermission` as a REQUIRED bound property (ControlManifest.Input.xml:32-37). Before the column can go, either the property becomes optional (the pill is hidden when unbound) and the communication form's control binding is updated, or the trio is removed from the communication form. The project, matter and work-assignment forms must keep binding and writing their own sprk_accesspermission unchanged.
- Contact coverage of communications (task 056, amended) must take the effective permission from the parent root's flags. This task records that rule in docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md, and the main session cross-links it into 056.
- The agent does NOT mutate live schema: code + docs + script only (owner directive recorded at task 038 / FAILURE-MODES AP-13).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no ctor null-check tests. Use the existing subclass-override doubles (FakeParticipationService, ThrowingFlagParticipationService) and the real NoAccessListReader / SubjectStandingGrantReader, as the task 044 seam suite does.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner binding: no Dataverse test in CI">Scope: live verification. It is a MANUAL gate run by hand on spaarkedev1 with the existing non-admin test users in the correct BU. Do NOT propose relocating users. No CI job gains a Dataverse credential.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR.
- State the placement decision (in the BFF: the evaluator and the grant core live there), citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md.
- Measure the publish-size delta against a FRESH master worktree using the short-path procedure (Compress-Archive; equal file counts on both sides). Report both sizes and the delta. Ceiling 60 MB.
- Run dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive: no new HIGH.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner binding">Scope: whole task. No scope cuts and nothing deferred. Scope discovered during execution is added to this task, not pushed to a follow-up.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <adr-tensions>
    <tension adr="ADR-003 (Amendment A1 evaluator contract)" path="B — amendment">
      <rule>"MUST let Secure (sprk_issecure) suppress derived-member + org-expansion BEFORE the max, for every principal kind" (.claude/adr/ADR-003-authorization-seams.md:39-40); full ADR item 8 (docs/adr/ADR-003-lean-authorization-seams.md:160-162).</rule>
      <conflict>The contract names Secure as the only pre-max suppressor. The owner's decision makes Limited suppress the same terms. Implementing it without amending the ADR would put a binding MUST out of step with the code.</conflict>
      <proposed>Amend item 8 to "Secure OR Limited (sprk_accesspermission = Limited) suppresses terms 3 and 4 and org-inherited grants BEFORE the max". Restricted stays a post-max veto. The concise edit is applied by the main session (sub-agent write boundary).</proposed>
      <rejected>Path A, a project-scoped exception: rejected, because Limited is permanent product semantics, not a project deviation. Path C, "comply by leaving Limited inert": rejected, because the owner has decided Limited must be real.</rejected>
    </tension>
  </adr-tensions>

  <justification>
    <existing>The write-time check: grep "GetRootRecordFlagsAsync" shows the only flag reader (ExternalParticipationService.cs:541). No write-time policy check exists anywhere in Api/ExternalAccess (GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:84-103 validates shape only). The retirement script: grep of scripts/ for "sprk_accesspermission" finds no retirement or column-delete script. The nearest pattern is scripts/Deploy-AccessEventEntity.ps1 (idempotent, -DryRun default, MSCRM.SolutionUniqueName).</existing>
    <extension>The check is a METHOD on the existing ExternalGrantLifecycle (the grant-lifecycle home), consuming the existing flag reader. It is not a new service or DI registration. The script follows Deploy-AccessEventEntity.ps1's shape. No existing script deletes a column or removes form references, so a new file is required.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the check, a Write-holder can mint a contact or org grant on a Restricted record, or an org-wide grant on a Secure record. /invite-and-grant also provisions a CIAM account and emails a person who can never get access. Without the script, the dead sprk_communication column stays on the form, where users can set a value that governs nothing, which contradicts owner Q6.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

