    <patterns>
      <pattern name="structural pre-max suppression" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:1258-1290">Extend the predicate; every term that consults it inherits Limited.</pattern>
      <pattern name="refusal before side effect" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/InviteAndGrantExternalUserEndpoint.cs:66-83">Root and expiry are validated before onboarding. The policy check joins them there.</pattern>
      <pattern name="designed banner state" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/AccessGrantModal/AccessGrantModal.tsx:1145-1168">Fluent v9 MessageBar with MessageBarTitle. Reuse for the Limited/Secure explanation (load the fluent-v9-component skill).</pattern>
      <pattern name="dry-run schema script" location="scripts/Deploy-AccessEventEntity.ps1">Idempotent, -DryRun default, solution-scoped, prefix-asserting.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Verify task 135 has merged, and that the CIAM strategy now consults GetRootRecordFlagsAsync and the shared veto pipeline. If it has not, STOP (escalation 1). Establish whether the C3 fix has landed (escalation 2).</step>
    <step order="1">Evaluator:
- Add the Limited signal to RootRecordFlags and populate it in GetRootRecordFlagsAsync.
- Replace the IsSecure-only suppression predicate with the direct-only predicate (Secure OR Limited) at both composition sites and in whatever CIAM composition task 135 left.
- Keep Unreadable as the most restrictive combination.
- Update comments that say "Secure" where the rule is now "Secure or Limited".</step>
    <step order="2">Write time:
- Add the one policy check (a method on ExternalGrantLifecycle). Call it before any side effect in /grant, /invite-and-grant and /invite.
- Make CreateGrantAsync refuse to write for a refused root.
- Return 422 ProblemDetails for refusals and a message-bearing ProblemDetails for a flag-read fault.
- Add the RecordAccessGateEndpoint remark explaining why the gate ignores the flags.</step>
    <step order="3">Dialog + PCF:
- Implement the effective-state mapping in pcf/TrackingFieldTrio/index.ts: accesspermission + sprk_issecure, with the gating read failing closed.
- Implement the per-state visibility rules in AccessGrantModal. Fix the Restricted contradiction so "+ User" stays enabled.
- Add the Limited/Secure banner, and surface the server's refusal detail.
- Make the pill honour the control's disabled state.
- Bump the PCF version in all four locations.</step>
    <step order="4">Communications:
- Enumerate EVERY reader and writer again (grep src/ plus a read-only live query of systemform formxml and savedquery layoutxml/fetchxml for sprk_communication.sprk_accesspermission and the TrackingFieldTrio control).
- Remove the code readers and writers. Update the Communication component tests.
- Make the TrackingFieldTrio manifest's accessPermission binding optional (or remove the trio from the communication form, per the scan), keeping the three root forms unchanged.
- Author the retirement script and run it with -DryRun only; record the output in notes.
- Update docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md.</step>
    <step order="5">ADR-003 amendment text for the full doc. Hand the concise edit to the main session with the exact replacement text in notes.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests per the acceptance criteria. Perturbation-check each new BFF assertion: disable the Limited predicate and the write-time check, and record which tests go red.</step>
    <step order="7">Build, unit + arch suites, jest for the two component libraries, PCF build:prod. Measure publish size (§10 procedure). Run the CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="8">Deploy the BFF to dev (bff-deploy skill) and the PCF (pcf-deploy skill), then run the manual live gate (acceptance criterion 16). Record results, including the two-user evidence, in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-138-access-permission-levels.md.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to `✅ [done]`. Document every deviation in the notes file.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>1. Task 135 has not merged, or its CIAM composition does not pass through the shared suppression/veto pipeline. STOP and do not add a CIAM-only Limited branch here; a second implementation is the drift C1 exists to remove. Escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
    <trigger>2. The C3 fix (grant cache round-trips DirectAccessLevel) has not landed. Direct grants on Limited or Secure roots then read as None on cache hits, and the live gate will show intermittent 403s for legitimately granted contacts. Do not work around it in this task (for example by bypassing the cache). Report the dependency and hold the live-gate sign-off until C3 is in.</trigger>
    <trigger>3. Owner Q5's "Assigned To" auto-grant function is owned by another task. If it writes grants on Limited or Secure records, it writes direct named contact grants, which this task ALLOWS; on Restricted it is refused. If the owner intends auto-grants to be suppressed on Limited (teams-app-r1 FR-14 said "no standing/auto"), that is a product decision. Surface it and do not guess. Recommendation: ALLOW them on Limited and Secure. They are named, direct grant rows an operator can see and remove (owner Q5), which is exactly what Limited admits; teams-app-r1's "no auto" meant derived membership, which this task suppresses. On Restricted the core refuses them with record_restricted; task 142 must treat that refusal as "skip and log", not as an error.</trigger>
    <trigger>4. The live form/view scan finds sprk_communication.sprk_accesspermission used by a managed-layer component, a business rule, a workflow or a plugin step that the script cannot remove. STOP before writing the delete step, and report the dependency with its solution layer.</trigger>
    <trigger>5. A communication surface turns out to need to DISPLAY the inherited parent permission (not merely stop writing its own). The recommended answer is to remove the control, since the parent's pill is the one place to change it. Adding an inherited read-only display is a product choice; ask before building it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

