  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">1. Evaluator, Limited, contact plane. On a Limited, non-secure, non-restricted root:
- a contact's org-inherited grant contributes nothing;
- its standing-grant membership contributes nothing;
- org expansion contributes nothing;
- its DIRECT grant contributes exactly its own level.
Asserted on the workforce contact plane and on the systemuser plane's contact-grants term, with the systemuser's ADR-034 membership term unaffected.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">2. Evaluator, Limited, CIAM plane. The same Limited root gives the same answer for a CIAM contact holding a direct grant, an org-inherited grant, or both. Asserted in CallerPrincipalResolverTests on task 135's pipeline.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">3. Secure behaviour is unchanged. Every pre-existing Secure/FR-22 seam and unit test passes. A root with BOTH Secure and Limited behaves identically to Secure.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">4. Restricted wins. A root that is Restricted (with or without Secure/Limited) gives ALL contact principals nothing, on the workforce contact plane, the CIAM plane and the systemuser plane's contact-grants term. The systemuser membership term survives.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">5. Fail closed. A flag row that is unreadable or not returned is treated as Restricted + direct-only (test through ThrowingFlagParticipationService). A null sprk_accesspermission is Standard (regression test). At WRITE time, a root id ABSENT from the returned flag map (for example, the flag read was called with an entity type that is not a RootFlagSources key) refuses with 503 `sdap.access.grant.policy_unreadable` and writes nothing. A table test pins ExternalGrantRootType → ExternalGrantRoot.LogicalNameFor → a flag-bearing entity type for project, matter and work assignment.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">6. Write time, Restricted. A caller WITH Write:
- /grant for a contact → 422 `sdap.access.grant.record_restricted` with a readable detail, and no sprk_externalrecordaccess row written;
- /grant for an organization → the same;
- /invite-and-grant → 422 before any contact create or CIAM provision (asserted: the provisioning seam is not reached);
- /invite → 422 with no contact or CIAM account created.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">7. Write time, Secure or Limited. An organization-wide grant (empty ContactId + OrganizationId) → 422 `sdap.access.grant.org_grant_direct_only_record` and no row. The positive twin, a named contact grant on the same root, succeeds. Both are asserted for a Secure root and for a Limited root.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">8. Shared core. Calling CreateGrantAsync directly for a Restricted root writes no row AND returns the typed refusal without throwing, so a future writer cannot bypass the check. The same call through the /grant route yields the 422 ProblemDetails, not the catch-all 500.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">9. Flag-read fault at write time. The request is refused with 503 `sdap.access.grant.policy_unreadable` and a human-readable detail. It is NOT reported as record_restricted, and it is distinguishable from a real Secure+Restricted record, which still gets 422 record_restricted (twin test). Nothing is written or provisioned. It is never an unhandled 500. The read path still treats the unreadable row as the most restrictive combination (criterion 5 stays green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">10. Authorization ordering (negative). A caller WITHOUT Write on a Restricted root receives the DelegationRuleFilter 403 (delegation_write_required), not the 422, so the record's access policy is not disclosed. /share-user by a Write-holder on Restricted, Limited and Secure roots still succeeds (positive), because internal access is unaffected.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">11. Dialog. Asserted by jest:
- Restricted: "+ Contact", "+ Organization" and candidate contact rows are NOT rendered. "+ User" is rendered and ENABLED. A staged user row's level dropdown and Add are enabled, and Add issues POST /share-user (asserted on the fetch mock's call list). Revoke on existing rows is enabled.
- Limited (which is also what a Secure record maps to): "+ Organization" is not rendered, and "+ Contact" and "+ User" are enabled.
- Standard: everything as before; the existing gating tests stay green, edited only where they pinned the old Restricted "+ User" block.
- Each non-standard state renders its explanatory MessageBar.
- A server 422 surfaces its detail text in the notice.
- The module doc comment no longer claims a standing-grant option is hidden.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">12. PCF mapping. Asserted as a pure-function test:
- accesspermission Restricted → 'restricted' (regardless of sprk_issecure);
- Limited → 'limited';
- Standard or null with sprk_issecure true → 'limited';
- Standard or null with sprk_issecure unreadable → 'limited';
- Standard or null with sprk_issecure false → 'standard'.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">13. Read-only honoured.
- The shared TrackingFieldTrio gains a disabled prop.
- The PCF sets it from `context.mode.isControlDisabled`, OR from the bound accessPermission attribute's `security.editable === false` (pill only), in init and in updateView.
- When disabled, the access-permission pill renders disabled and its menu cannot open, and onAccessPermissionChange is never called (jest, with the prop both true and false). The High Priority and Monitor controls in the same row honour the same prop (the same defect, fixed here).
- Enabled behaviour is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">14. Communications, code. grep over src/ finds no reader or writer of sprk_communication.sprk_accesspermission: EMAIL_TRACKING_FIELDS.accessPermission, updateAccessPermission and the EmailTrackingPanel access props are removed, with their tests updated. The PCF comments no longer call the root option values "sprk_communication" values. docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md records the retirement and the inherit-from-parent rule.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">15. Communications, schema.
- The retirement script exists and defaults to -DryRun.
- It is idempotent: a second run reports nothing to do.
- It removes form, view and PCF-binding references before the column delete.
- Its dry-run output against spaarkedev1 is recorded in the notes.
- The operator's real run is part of the manual gate (criterion 16).
- The TrackingFieldTrio manifest no longer REQUIRES an accessPermission binding (or the trio is gone from the communication form, per the live scan). A jest/PCF test shows the control rendering without the pill when the property is unbound. Project, matter and work-assignment forms still bind, read and write their own sprk_accesspermission (asserted by the existing TrackingFieldTrio tests plus one new unbound case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">16. MANUAL LIVE GATE on spaarkedev1, run by hand with existing non-admin test users in the correct BU and an existing test contact identity, results recorded in notes:
(a) Restricted project: "+ User" shares a colleague; the contact/org options are absent; a forced /grant returns the 422 message; a contact holding a prior grant loses access on Teams and on the external SPA; an internal user with role access keeps it.
(b) Limited project: an org-inherited-only contact loses access; a directly granted contact keeps its level; "+ Organization" is absent.
(c) Secure non-restricted project: behaves as (b).
(d) Standard project: unchanged. Plus (verifier r1 finding 7): on the project, matter AND work-assignment main forms under PCF v1.0.32 the access-permission pill still renders and still writes (change the value, save, confirm sprk_accesspermission round-trips on each form); on a secure record the closed pill reads "Secure" in red and its menu is Standard / Limited / Restricted.
(e) The communication form no longer shows an access-permission control after the operator runs the retirement script.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">17. The ADR-003 amendment text (full doc) is merged in this PR and names Limited alongside Secure. The concise-ADR replacement text is recorded in the notes and handed to the main session. The PR description carries the §6.5 path-B citation. The owner's approval of the amendment is recorded in the PR before merge (§6.5: the human reviewer chooses the path).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">18. docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-ADMIN-SETUP.md carries the Standard / Limited / Restricted × Secure matrix, stating which grant types each admits and which plane enforces it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">19. Build green. BFF unit + integration (seam) + NetArchTest green. jest green for Spaarke.UI.Components and Spaarke.Communication.Components. The Communication.Components consumers still type-check and build after the hook/export removals (src/solutions/EmailPage and Spaarke.AI.Widgets' EmailWorkspaceWidget). PCF build:prod green. Publish-size delta reported per §10 (fresh master worktree, short path, equal file counts), ≤ 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">20. Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above (Limited × each term × each plane, Restricted precedence, fail-closed flags, write-time refusals incl. ordering, dialog state matrix, PCF mapping). Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

